From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 18:42:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: align HW1 native four-address RX headers

QCN9274 HW1 WBE.1.0 pads a native-WiFi four-address header from 30 to
32 bytes. Pulling only the IEEE 802.11 header leaves two padding bytes
before LLC/SNAP. A WDS AP then exposes malformed Ethernet frames and the
wired client behind the station cannot resolve ARP.

Remove the hardware padding before rebuilding the QoS and crypto fields,
when the padding and SNAP header are both present. Some receive paths
already strip the padding, so an unconditional alignment would corrupt
those frames. Select by HW1 and frame format; leave other RX intact.

On BE10000 ES as the WDS AP, enabling alignment in the same temporary
module restores ARP, bidirectional traffic, timed PTK renewal and station
reconnect. Disabling alignment reproduces malformed LLC/SNAP and ARP loss.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -989,7 +989,18 @@
 	/* pull decapped header */
 	hdr = (struct ieee80211_hdr *)msdu->data;
 	hdr_len = ieee80211_hdrlen(hdr->frame_control);
-	skb_pull(msdu, hdr_len);
+	/* WBE.1.0 can retain alignment after a native four-address header.
+	 * Some receive paths already remove it; require padding plus SNAP
+	 * rather than stripping two bytes from every HW1 WDS frame.
+	 */
+	if (dp_pdev->dp->ab->hw_rev == ATH12K_HW_QCN9274_HW10 &&
+	    ieee80211_has_a4(hdr->frame_control) && hdr_len % 4 &&
+	    msdu->len >= ALIGN(hdr_len, 4) + 6 &&
+	    !get_unaligned_le16(msdu->data + hdr_len) &&
+	    !memcmp(msdu->data + ALIGN(hdr_len, 4), "\xaa\xaa\x03\x00\x00", 5))
+		skb_pull(msdu, ALIGN(hdr_len, 4));
+	else
+		skb_pull(msdu, hdr_len);
 
 	/*  Rebuild qos header */
 	hdr->frame_control |= __cpu_to_le16(IEEE80211_STYPE_QOS_DATA);
